  "summary": "Three intermeshing screws turn in a closely fitted housing: a centre power rotor driven by the motor and two idler rotors driven by the liquid pressure acting on their threads. The meshing threads create a series of sealed chambers that move steadily from the inlet end to the outlet end as the rotors turn, giving smooth, nearly pulse-free flow and quiet running at high pressures. Suited to clean lubricating liquids — lube and seal oil, fuel oil, hydraulic oil.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive displacement – rotary",
    "configuration": "Three-screw, untimed (idlers hydraulically driven), single suction"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "rotor_proportions": "Power rotor OD 5/3·d, root d; idler OD d, root d/3 (classic ratios)",
    "lead": "≈10/3·d (representative)",
    "thread_profile_note": "True rotors use conjugate cycloidal profiles; the model approximates them for visual study."
  },
